Subject: [PATCH 54/57] fix: the mode 3 panel border is measured in
 panel-relative uv

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01A72MFkdSczncE7au9UVnmu
---
 Engine/Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/HDRPostProcess.cfx | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Engine/Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/HDRPostProcess.cfx b/Engine/Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/HDRPostProcess.cfx
index 89ecc739..f2be8573 100644
--- a/Engine/Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/HDRPostProcess.cfx
+++ b/Engine/Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/HDRPostProcess.cfx
@@ -641,8 +641,8 @@ float4 DiffractionDebugPS(vtxOut IN) : SV_Target
 		// visible WHETHER OR NOT anything cleared the threshold. Without it "no sources" and
 		// "the debug pass never ran" are the same black rectangle, which is the one confusion a
 		// diagnostic must not have.
-		const float2 vBorder = max(DiffractionDebugParams.xy * 0.004, 1e-5);
-		const bool bBorder = any(uv < vBorder) || any(uv > (1.0 - vBorder));
+		const float fBorder = 0.004;  // panel-relative, so about two pixels of a 480 px panel
+		const bool bBorder = any(uv < fBorder) || any(uv > (1.0 - fBorder));
 		float e = bBorder ? 0.12 : 0.03;
 
 		// Four decades of grey above that floor, and any excess at all starts a quarter of the
